{"text": "isle", "etymologies": [{"etymologyHTML": "<p>From Middle English <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"enm\">ile</i>, <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"enm\">yle</i> (with <i>s</i> added, similar to English <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\">island</i>), borrowed from Old French <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"fro\">ille</i>, <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"fro\">idle</i>, <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"fro\">isle</i>, from Latin <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"la\">insula</i>. Not related to <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\">island</i>. Doublet of <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\">insula</i>.\n</p>", "pos": [{"pos": "Noun", "definitions": [{"definition": "An island, usually very small. Compare with islet.", "quote": [], "relative": {}}]}]}, {"etymologyHTML": "<p>isle (<i>plural</i> <b class=\"Latn form-of lang-en p-form-of\" lang=\"en\">isles</b>)\n</p>", "pos": [{"pos": "Noun", "definitions": [{"definition": "Obsolete spelling of aisle.", "quote": [], "relative": {}}]}]}], "pronunciation": [["UK, US", "/a\u026a\u032fl/"]]}